### Expected behavior
the chunked size is calculated correctly

### Actual behavior
java.lang.NumberFormatException is thrown

### Steps to reproduce

See code below.

Please be aware that I'm not at all familiar with the netty code. Added a few comments in the code below.

### Minimal yet complete reproducer code (or URL to code)

```
import io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;

public class JavaTester {

     private static int getChunkSizeNewFixed(byte[] hex, int start, int length) {
        // byte[] is produced by LineParse::parseLine that already skip ISO CTRL and Whitespace chars
        // COMMENT: ^ I could see handling for control chars but not whitespaces ^, but maybe I'm missing something.
        int result = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
            final int digit = StringUtil.decodeHexNibble(hex[start + i]);
            if (digit == -1) {
                // COMMENT: Until version 4.1.87.final the whitespace and control char checks where in there
                if (hex[start + i] == ';' || Character.isWhitespace(hex[start + i])) {
                    return result;
                }
                throw new NumberFormatException();
            }
            result *= 16;
            result += digit;
        }
        return result;
    }

    private static int getChunkSizeNew(byte[] hex, int start, int length) {
        // byte[] is produced by LineParse::parseLine that already skip ISO CTRL and Whitespace chars
        int result = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
            final int digit = StringUtil.decodeHexNibble(hex[start + i]);
            if (digit == -1) {
                // uncommon path
                if (hex[start + i] == ';') {
                    return result;
                }
                throw new NumberFormatException();
            }
            result *= 16;
            result += digit;
        }
        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String... args) {
        String toTest = "BDC Cookie: NSC_wTfswfs_c2cjoufhsbujpo=ffffffff099b5f1f45525d5f4f58455e445a4a42378b;expires=Mon, 13-Mar-2023 14:16:06 GMT;path=/;secure;httponly";
        System.out.println(getChunkSizeNewFixed(toTest.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8), 0, 4));
        System.out.println(getChunkSizeNew(toTest.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8), 0, 4)); <-- throws NumberFormatException
    }
}
```


### Netty version

from 4.1.88 onwards.

### JVM version (e.g. `java -version`)
openjdk version "1.8.0_292"
OpenJDK Runtime Environment (AdoptOpenJDK)(build 1.8.0_292-b10)


### OS version (e.g. `uname -a`)
MacOS and Ubuntu
